Local commit: `8c173b6b3f0fbd9e99872722f774371310b828b3`

Exact patch hash (`git diff 9ad1999b 8c173b6b | git hash-object --stdin`):
`2f2e52b549e3bb2e8b4b20ccb75e51d5520df5da`

## Result

- Preserved the prior uncommitted fixes: process-wide child-wait state across
  worker exec, visible ENOTSUP for unsupported Tool-owned worker exec, the full
  proc-exe alias cross-product, and Linux-width comm truncation.
- Added mutex-backed CLONE_FS state (`cwd`, `cwd_fd`, `umask`) and
  CLONE_SIGHAND state shared by KVM thread executors. Fork children receive
  private snapshots. Exec refreshes the latest process-wide state, applies
  Linux signal-disposition reset rules, and republishes the post-exec state.
- Added a leader-exec admission check ordered by the same mutex as synchronous
  process-child entry. A leader now receives ENOTSUP before image mutation when
  a worker is running a child whose separate GuestThreadGroup cannot be
  cancelled. Process-action plumbing reports whether replacement actually
  occurred, avoiding a false Tool post-exec event on refusal.
- Extended that plumbing to report the effective raw syscall result as well as
  image replacement. A Tool-intercepted leader exec refusal now propagates
  ENOTSUP through `complete_injection`, `KvmGuest::inject`, and `tail_inject`
  instead of letting the handler's earlier prepared `Ok(0)` overwrite it.
- Added end-to-end coverage for post-clone cwd/umask/SIGUSR1-ignore inheritance
  through worker exec and for the Tool-intercepted inverse
  leader-exec/worker-child deadlock. The latter uses `ThreadOwnership::Host`
  with `PostExecTool`, asserts exactly one post-exec call, and has a five-second
  host-side fuse so a regression fails instead of hanging indefinitely. Added
  a focused coordination unit test as well.

