- `cargo test -p reverie-kvm --test static_elf nonleader_exec_observes_post_clone_fs_and_sighand_updates -- --exact --nocapture --test-threads=1` — pass (1/1, 0.14s final focused run).
- `cargo test -p reverie-kvm --test static_elf leader_exec_fails_visibly_while_a_worker_runs_a_direct_fork_child -- --exact --nocapture` — pass (1/1, 0.50s final focused run).
- `cargo test -p reverie-kvm -- --test-threads=1` — pass: 273 tests total (209 unit, 64 integration); static_elf 50/50 in 12.48s, 16.39s wall clock including build and doc tests.
- `cargo clippy -p reverie-kvm --all-targets -- -D warnings` — pass (2.12s).
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` — pass.
- `git diff --check` — pass before the amended commit.

## Mutation evidence

- Removed only cwd/cwd_fd propagation: shared-state E2E failed with guest exit 40.
- Removed only umask propagation: shared-state E2E failed with guest exit 42.
- Detached only signal-disposition sharing: shared-state E2E failed with guest exit 43.
- Disabled only leader-exec admission: inverse E2E hit its five-second deadlock
  fuse and failed. All mutations were reverted before final gates and commit.
- Discarded only the process action's effective result in `KvmGuest::inject`:
  the Tool-owned inverse E2E failed with guest exit 12 instead of 0, after its
  one-post-exec-call assertion passed. The mutation was restored before gates.

## Residual limitation

Leader exec is deliberately refused with ENOTSUP while any sibling is in the
synchronous direct process-child path; the backend still does not propagate
cancellation into that nested child's separate GuestThreadGroup. Tool-driven
non-leader exec remains explicitly unsupported and returns ENOTSUP, as before.

