## Exact-head review repairs at 8c173b6b

### Changes

- Child-process joining now runs only when the exiting executor is the thread
  group leader. A normal CLONE_THREAD worker neither joins the shared process
  children nor cancels its siblings. All five normal Tool exit paths use the
  same guarded helper: exit from thread start, exit from initial exec handling,
  exit from initial post-exec handling, an observed exit-group request, and
  exit from the main syscall loop.
- Synthetic `/proc/self/stat` and `/proc/self/status` now append the first 15
  `comm` bytes directly. No UTF-8 decoding or replacement can expand or alter
  those bytes.

### Verification

- `cargo test -p reverie-kvm executor::tests:: --lib -- --test-threads=1`:
  162/162 passed.
- `cargo test -p reverie-kvm runtime::tests:: --lib -- --test-threads=1`:
  9/9 passed.
- `cargo test -p reverie-kvm --test static_elf
  tool_worker_exit_does_not_wait_for_process_child -- --exact --nocapture
  --test-threads=1`: 1/1 passed in 0.17 seconds; a restored confirmation passed
  in 0.32 seconds.
- `cargo test --workspace --all-features --no-run`: passed.
- `cargo clippy -p reverie-kvm --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check`: passed.

### Mutation evidence

- Replacing only the guarded process-exit join in the main Tool loop with the
  former unconditional join made the real KVM test hit its five-second bound
  and fail in 5.16 seconds. Restoring the guard returned it to 1/1 passing.
- Removing the same guard inside the non-KVM child-wait test made that test
  hit its one-second bound and fail. Restoring it returned the test to passing.
- Reintroducing lossy UTF-8 conversion in both synthetic proc consumers made
  `proc_comm_preserves_raw_bytes_and_linux_width` fail on the 15-byte name
  ending in byte ff. Restoring direct byte insertion returned it to passing.

