## Process-exit callback repair at 8c173b6b

### Change

- `notify_tool_exit` always delivers `Tool::on_exit_thread`, but it now delivers
  `Tool::on_exit_process` only when the exiting executor is the thread-group
  leader. A normal CLONE_THREAD worker therefore cannot consume the process-wide
  Tool state or report process exit while its leader continues.
- The existing real worker-exit test now calls `getpid` after joining its worker
  and before releasing its process child. The Tool asserts that the root process
  has received zero process-exit callbacks at that point, then the final result
  asserts exactly one callback for the root and one for the fork child.

### Exit-path enumeration

- The shared helper has seven callers: five normal termination paths (exit from
  thread start, initial exec handling, initial post-exec handling, an observed
  thread-group exit, and the main syscall loop) plus two post-exec error paths.
- The separate single-root `run_with_tool` HLT path calls the thread and process
  callbacks directly. It cannot host a CLONE_THREAD worker and is unchanged.

### Callback-consumer enumeration

- Interface/default: `reverie/src/tool.rs`.
- KVM: `reverie-kvm/src/runtime.rs`, `reverie-kvm/src/tools.rs`, and
  `reverie-kvm/tests/static_elf.rs`.
- ptrace: `reverie-ptrace/src/task.rs` and `reverie-ptrace/src/tracer.rs`.
- DBT: `reverie-dbt/src/lib.rs` and `reverie-dbt/src/tools.rs`.
- LiteInst: `reverie-liteinst/src/tool_host.rs`,
  `reverie-liteinst/src/bin/rpc_tool_guest.rs`, and
  `reverie-liteinst/tests/hybrid.rs`.
- SaBRe and e9patch: `experimental/reverie-sabre/src/reverie_adapter.rs` and
  `reverie-e9patch/src/tool_host.rs`.
- Examples and common tests: `reverie-examples/strace/tool.rs`,
  `reverie-examples/counter2_tool.rs`, `tests/state.rs`, `tests/exit.rs`, and
  `tests/busywait.rs`.

